      "writtenOn": "2023-02-09T02:18:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just check the latest mainline code, there no vendor module(out of pcie-designware.c or pcie-designware-host.c) use iatu_unroll_enabled or io_cfg_atu_shared till these two variable rename, so I don\u0027t think this change could be a break to vendor module.",
      "revId": "ceab4f6bc80c80d9feace8e2e614691a6bd7549c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eaf5bf2d_1f84d347",
        "filename": "drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 610,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T18:36:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "doesn\u0027t this break vendor modules that don\u0027t know about DWC_IATU_IOCFG_SHARED? For example, if a vendor module has a test like like 499:\n```\nif (!ret \u0026\u0026 pci-\u003eio_cfg_atu_shared)\n```\nthey will assume that this flag means IOCFG_SHARED, won\u0027t it?",
      "revId": "ceab4f6bc80c80d9feace8e2e614691a6bd7549c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f1e919d_e28a79af",
        "filename": "drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 610,
      "author": {
        "id": 1659389
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-09T02:16:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, this doesn\u0027t break vendor modules.\nThe pci-\u003eiatu_unroll_enabled logic are all handle in \"pcie-designware.c\" and \"pcie-designware-host.c\" which are both inside the GKI. So this change has nothing to do with the vendor modules .",
      "parentUuid": "eaf5bf2d_1f84d347",
      "revId": "ceab4f6bc80c80d9feace8e2e614691a6bd7549c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3126ff9f_9df21a49",
        "filename": "drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 610,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-09T18:49:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So you are saying that no vendor module will ever look at io_cfg_atu_shared or use IOCFG_SHARED. How can you be confident of that? I\u0027m not.\n\nHow about setting DWC_IATU_IOCFG_SHARED in a vendor hook so it is completely compatible? All of the tests can stay since the bit will only be set via vendor hook.\n\nThis should be squashed with asop/2378292 (turned into \"BACKPORT\")",
      "parentUuid": "2f1e919d_e28a79af",
      "revId": "ceab4f6bc80c80d9feace8e2e614691a6bd7549c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
